# Regression test: `units electron` conversion factors.
#
# pair_style zero makes this an ideal gas, so the velocities never change and
# T_vac (from equipartition on VACF(0)) must reproduce the temperature that
# `velocity create` imposed.  Any error in vac_to_jmol or dt_to_ps shows up
# directly in column 8 (T_vac) of ELEC.thermo.
#
#   expected : T_vac ~= 300 K  (sampling scatter of a few K on 125 atoms)
#   regression: 5.09e5 K, i.e. 1709x high, when the electron velocity unit is
#               mistaken for Bohr/atu instead of Bohr/fs
#
# LAMMPS defines the electron time unit as the femtosecond
# (update.cpp: force->femtosecond = 1.0, dt = 0.001) and its velocity unit by
# force->mvv2e = 1.06657236, which solves to 5.291772e4 m/s = 1 Bohr/fs.

units           electron
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p

lattice         sc 5.0
region          box block 0 5 0 5 0 5
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 39.948

pair_style      zero 10.0
pair_coeff      * *

velocity        all create 300.0 12345 mom yes dist gaussian
fix             1 all nve
fix             2 all xpt 1 256 ELEC

timestep        0.001
thermo          128
thermo_style    custom step temp f_2[7]
run             300
